====Far C====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=jaehoon_fC
|description=Jae Hoon does a far-reaching roundhouse kick that only slightly advances his body. Exceptional poke, Jae Hoon's main way of space trapping and whiff punishing opponents and walling them out. Cancelling into a super is the only way to convert off a hit but a Wild Punish can allow for a follow-up from any range, depending on the option. 
* Prone to getting hopped over if done too late.
* Can be linked from Wild Punish with a walk > clD, walk > 2C or REV Hangetsuzan.
*Usually safe when spaced out, but is always -6 on block. Quite easily punished if not spaced well
}}

====Far D====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=jaehoon_fD
|description=Jae Hoon advances while up kicking, hitting twice. Essential button for Jae Hoon as it uniquely leaves him slightly advantageous letting him continue offense without REV from a far heavy. Although far D has a massive weakness of hit not immediately hitting crouchers, it enforces Jae Hoon's rushdown and is one of his best ways of closing the gap and extending pressure.This button is also super cancelable.
* One of the strongest buttons in the game
* Links into 2A on hit and 2C on counterhit.
* Hits the highest out of his far pokes making it great for catching jumps early. 
* Only hits crouching opponents on frame 23 as the first hit does not hit crouchers.
**This leaves Jae Hoon vulnerable to 2Cs from almost any character, often leading to a devastating close-range wild punish.

WARNING: Despite the amazing upsides to this button, it has alot of counterplay and weaknesses that could lose you the game. The main one being being very suseptible to  high dodge attacks getting hopped on and whiff-punished due to the high recovery. Being predictable with this button can be extremely costly. 
}}

